WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:03.960
Chris Pratt wasn't always the ripped action
star he is today.

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:08.710
Every year, it gets harder and harder to remember
that his big break was playing chubby but

00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:12.530
lovable Andy Dwyer on NBC's Parks and Recreation.

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:14.799
"Andy is our official water fountain tester"

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:17.000
"Alright, let's give this sucker a test drive."

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:23.980
How did he slim down and muscle up to become
Star-Lord?

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:28.390
Here's a look behind the scenes of Chris Pratt's
insane workouts.

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:29.390
Workout rollercoaster

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:34.430
As impressive as the transformation was, playing
Star-Lord wasn't the first time Pratt modified

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:35.930
his body for a role.

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:40.420
His bulbous weight as Andy was a deliberate
choice, and he lost a lot of it to develop

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:43.649
a believable baseball player's physique for
Moneyball.

00:00:43.649 --> 00:00:48.610
Then he bulked up even more to play a tier-one
operator for Zero Dark Thirty, and immediately

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:54.980
after that, he gained 60 pounds of pure gut
to play opposite Vince Vaughn in 2013's Delivery

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:55.980
Man.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:01:01.280
"This is you as the SEAL, and then this is
you very shortly afterwards."

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:04.800
Chris Pratt told Vulture in 2012:

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.930
"I just like to gain weight and lose weight.

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:08.930
It's a rollercoaster.

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:10.400
I just want to do this.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.840
I want to touch God."

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:17.060
After that he started cutting down again for
Marvel, and now that he's in Star-Lord shape,

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:19.759
it looks like he intends to stay there.

00:01:19.759 --> 00:01:20.790
Cold turkey

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:25.190
Anyone who drinks knows that one of the lousiest
side effects of alcohol is the hit to your

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:27.350
waistline from all the empty calories.

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:28.340
Plus, hangovers.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:30.820
"Oh my God I'm so hungover.

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:33.000
I've never been this hungover.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.310
Are we dead?"

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:38.610
Unsurprisingly, part of Pratt's weight-loss
routine involved cutting alcohol out of his

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:42.260
diet, which he did until the first Guardians
of the Galaxy was complete.

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:46.860
He told Jay Leno, "I didn't drink for seven
or eight months, which was really not that

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:47.860
difficult for me.

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:52.000
I'm not like a huge alcoholic or anything,
but I always prided myself on being in a pretty

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.000
good mood.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:57.430
And then I stopped drinking alcohol for eight
months, and I realize from time to time I

00:01:57.430 --> 00:01:59.060
got grumpy."

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:02.960
Considering where it got him, it was probably
worth the sacrifice.

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:03.960
Good eats

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:08.300
He may make it look effortless, but Pratt's
body transformations haven't always been smooth

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:09.300
sailing.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:13.379
While preparing for his role as a Seal Team
6 member in Zero Dark Thirty, Pratt tried

00:02:13.379 --> 00:02:17.260
to brute-force his way to a ripped physique
while starving himself.

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:20.360
While it worked in the short term, it definitely
wasn't good for him.

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:22.180
He told People in 2014:

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:27.870
"I was doing 500 pushups a day, working out
at the gym, running five miles a day, but

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:30.400
with no food, and I tore my body apart.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:35.030
I felt terrible afterwards, had to get shoulder
surgery, and I wore myself down doing that

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:36.920
because I didn't have the proper coaching."

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:41.180
Worse, after all that effort, the weight just
came right back.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:45.200
It wasn't until he started eating properly
and following a plan he could sustain that

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:46.510
he found a sweet spot.

00:02:46.510 --> 00:02:48.410
No more yo-yo dieting for this guy.

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:52.120
"All I've had is fruits and vegetables for
weeks now.

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:53.400
Mmm.

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:55.800
Oh, my God!"

00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:58.760
Insane workouts

00:02:58.769 --> 00:03:03.540
Dropping 60 pounds in six months — and keeping
it off — is no walk in the park.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:08.300
It takes everyday focus and determination,
or as Pratt put it, "Three or four hours a

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:11.190
day of just consistent, ass-kicking hard work."

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.660
But he wasn't on his own.

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:17.909
Marvel producers hand-picked a personal trainer
for Pratt: Duffy Gaver, a former Navy SEAL

00:03:17.909 --> 00:03:20.750
who's made a specialty out of getting actors
into shape.

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:25.760
As Gaver describes his training philosophy,
"It's less about the workout and more about

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:29.690
what you bring to the workout — your will,
your desire, your discipline.

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:32.590
If it was easy, everyone would be in shape."

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:34.819
So what kinds of workouts was he doing?

00:03:34.819 --> 00:03:36.150
Well…all of them.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:41.810
Heavy lifts, swimming, mountain biking, cardio,
rowing, calisthenics — four to six workouts

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:42.810
a week.

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:47.269
On top of that, Pratt worked in some P90X
and Crossfit, because why not?

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:50.000
It's enough to make your body hurt just thinking
about it.

00:03:57.860 --> 00:03:59.920
From Star-Lord to Ironman

00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:06.670
Speaking of "because why not?," in 2015, Pratt
competed in his first Ironman 70.3, a grueling

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:13.959
70.3 mile triathlon that saw Pratt swim 1.2
miles, bike 56 miles, and run 13.1 miles,

00:04:13.959 --> 00:04:17.780
for a total of just over seven hours of pain.

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:21.690
Though fine-tuning his physique was surely
a part of the reason he took the challenge,

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:26.380
his main motivation was to support fellow
participant Mike Day, a retired Navy SEAL

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:28.840
who was once severely wounded in combat.

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:33.330
After the race, Pratt told Ironman, "Mike
Day's story is just so incredible.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:38.840
I figured if a guy who's been shot 27 times
can tough this race out I had no excuse."

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:40.270
Eyes on the prize

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:44.720
Anybody who's ever tried to diet or stick
to a workout plan knows it's an easy train

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:45.720
to fall from.

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:49.820
A couple of skipped days, a cheat meal or
two, and before you know it you're right back

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:51.340
to riding scooters to the bathroom.

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:55.290
But Pratt had a pretty powerful incentive
to show up for his workouts.

00:04:55.290 --> 00:05:00.570
"... book a Marvel movie and have a deadline,
and then it's like if you don't, if you get

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:01.590
fat, you might get fired.

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:02.740
And then it's easy, heh heh."

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:07.190
Of course, that doesn't come close to conveying
how seriously Pratt took the exercise.

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:12.220
According to his trainer, Duffy Gaver, "Chris'
athleticism is amazing," "He is incredibly

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:14.800
disciplined and his work ethic is phenomenal.

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:20.130
[...] He isn't the client you have to push;
he's the type of client you have to pull down."

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:25.190
Intense and focused, Pratt came into his training
knowing exactly what he wanted: to entertain

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:29.300
filmgoers as the best Star-Lord he could possibly
be.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:30.930
"Oh, I'm sorry.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.240
I didn't know how this machine worked."

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:33.380
Thanks for watching!

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:36.759
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:36.759 --> 00:05:39.469
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

